To find each value of $\maroonD y$, we need to take each value of $\greenD x$, $\blueD{\text{ multiply it by }6}$ and then $\goldE{\text{subtract } 4} $.

For example, when $\greenD {x} = \greenD{1}$:

$\begin{align}
\maroonD{y} &= \greenD{1}\blueD{\times6}\goldE{-4} \\\\
\maroonD{y} &= \maroonD{2}
\end{align}$
